     "9c1e20ea-10db-4252-bb12-29eb8511ce42"], Cell[
    "quotients of the hyperbolic tiling", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e3fd4757-f397-4257-a67d-abae50ca06f6"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"982ccb27-8156-44d5-bf05-\
b81a72d94f77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Euler characteristic ",
 StyleBox["V", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["F", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["F", "TI"],
 " = 2",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " reads the surface off the graph: 2 on the sphere, 0 on the torus, negative \
on a hyperbolic surface."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0b016edb-888b-4b76-a45d-f1d5a11cb44f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every map here is ",
 StyleBox["closed",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". A line or a circle drawn on it wraps round the surface, and on a small \
map the wrap is felt within a few steps. For plane geometry use the patches \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrate"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrate", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ff5f3703-d5d9-4701-8347-b87572da2225"],
 ", which are cut from the infinite tiling and have no wrap."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7529b3e3-a6ca-4a09-bd4e-99344b259f99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The flat tori are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TorusTessellation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/TorusTessellation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "310dfa44-9dbd-442a-bba7-99eb4ad40bfc"],
 " graphs. The uniform maps are built with the Conway operations on a regular \
seed: rectify, truncate and their composites. Apart from the snub cube and \
the snub dodecahedron, the snub and elongated families are not built, and \
give ",
 Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec961dd0-c615-4e5d-8361-244766d6113c"],
 " with a message."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"76afed05-9ee9-41c3-8cb6-1a4230fbabba"],

